{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `y` is a top-level data variable and is scored exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement. All parameters have built-in prior sampling statements before they are used in the likelihood, and the remaining data variables are context inputs.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  real x0; // Baseline input

  int<lower=1> N; // Number of observations
  vector[N] x; // Observed inputs
  vector[N] y; // Observed outputs

  int<lower=1> N_grid; // Number of grid points
  array[N_grid] real x_grid;  // Input grid
}

transformed data {
  vector[N] delta_x;
  vector[N] delta_x2;
  vector[N] delta_x3;

  for (n in 1:N) {
    delta_x[n] = x[n] - x0;
    delta_x2[n] = pow(delta_x[n], 2.0);
    delta_x3[n] = pow(delta_x[n], 3.0);
  }
}

parameters {
  real alpha;  // Intercept
  real beta1;  // First-order slope
  real beta2;  // Second-order slope
  real beta3;  // Third-order slope
  real<lower=0> sigma; // Measurement Variability
}

model {
  alpha ~ normal(0, 3);
  beta1 ~ normal(0, 1);
  beta2 ~ normal(0, 1);
  beta3 ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma ~ normal(0, 1);

  y ~ normal(  alpha
             + beta1 * delta_x
             + beta2 * delta_x2
             + beta3 * delta_x3, sigma);
}

generated quantities {
  array[N] real y_pred;
  array[N_grid] real mu_grid;
  array[N_grid] real y_pred_grid;

  for (n in 1:N)
    y_pred[n] = normal_rng(  alpha
                           + beta1 * delta_x[n]
                           + beta2 * delta_x2[n]
                           + beta3 * delta_x3[n], sigma);

  for (n in 1:N_grid) {
    mu_grid[n] =   alpha
                 + beta1 * (x_grid[n] - x0)
                 + beta2 * pow(x_grid[n] - x0, 2.0)
                 + beta3 * pow(x_grid[n] - x0, 3.0);
    y_pred_grid[n] = normal_rng(mu_grid[n], sigma);
  }
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":1,"N_grid":4,"x":[4.757900665279479],"x0":6.550673297580628,"x_grid":[1.0,2.0,3.0,4.0],"y":[1.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
